+## OpenStorm .171 literal Kernel alias precedence
+
+Effective alias navigation honors standard Kernel modern-over-legacy property
+precedence and last decoded string keys in literal arrays/spreads. Shared
+constructor/synchronization ownership gates cross-property priority. Inherited
+and trait declarations retain their own locations, and possible Kernel roots
+remain separate. Unknown maps, integer merge keys, custom lifecycle methods and
+ambiguous composition retain incomplete alternatives. Physical class strings
+remain checked-rename inputs even when their alias declaration is shadowed.
+Contributed by @thinkycz.
