 **Impact: Medium · Complexity: Medium**
 
+Literal string-key maps now honor modern-over-legacy property precedence and
+last decoded keys in literal array/spread order, when shared method ownership
+proves the standard Kernel constructor/synchronization model. Inherited and trait
+property owners retain their locations; each possible selected Kernel keeps its
+own precedence. Physical class-string references remain transformation inputs.
+Custom lifecycle methods, opaque/numeric-key maps and ambiguous origins remain
+incomplete. These static priorities do not model callback/property mutations.
+
 Resolve runtime-built alias maps and property mutations without executing bootstrap
 code. Prove compatible multiple-trait declarations before enabling transformations;
 otherwise keep all known source origins and explicit incomplete/ambiguous metadata.
